  "phase": "DEFINE",
  "minute": 116.0,
  "event_seq": 263,
  "root_problem": "Dispute ticket volume doubled from ~600/month (Jun-Jul) to ~1220+/month (Aug-Sep 2026) (E-05). The dominant identified driver is billing-import validation rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01, which flags high consumption by comparing the raw AMI register value directly against 12-month m3 usage history with no unit scaling (E-12); because firmware v4.2 meters (rollout June 2026) report reads in a native register unit of \"0.1 m3\" rather than \"m3\" (E-13), BV-17 misflags their valid high-but-correct consumption as anomalous and rejects the read at import (REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION), forcing estimate substitution. This pathway explains 1184 of the 1240 disputed ESTIMATED-read bills (E-11); the cause of the larger segment of disputes tied to ACTUAL metered reads (1785 of 3025, E-03) is not yet established and is not assumed to share this mechanism."
 },
